WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.740 --> 00:00:02.560
The Russo Brothers are back at it again.

00:00:02.730 --> 00:00:06.260
In the days leading up to their appearance
at this year's San Diego Comic-Con, which

00:00:06.279 --> 00:00:11.800
takes place from July 18 to July 21, Avengers:
Infinity War and Avengers: Endgame directors

00:00:11.800 --> 00:00:15.629
Joe and Anthony Russo have taken to social
media to tease what they'll be showing off

00:00:15.629 --> 00:00:18.000
at the highly anticipated entertainment convention.

00:00:18.120 --> 00:00:22.240
What started off simply has turned into something
much bigger, and fans are going absolutely

00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:24.520
bonkers over the Russos' most recent tease.

00:00:24.700 --> 00:00:29.339
Things began innocently when the sibling filmmakers
shared an Instagram photo of the San Diego

00:00:29.339 --> 00:00:33.310
Comic-Con logo as a way to confirm that they'd
be presenting their own panel "A Conversation

00:00:33.310 --> 00:00:38.160
with the Russo Brothers," which will be held
on Friday, July 19 at 11 AM PST.

00:00:38.220 --> 00:00:44.160
Then, the teasing evolved when the Russo Brothers
shared a video with text that read "07/19/19"

00:00:44.170 --> 00:00:48.800
and background audio from 2017's San Diego
Comic-Con, where a snippet of Avengers: Infinity

00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:50.900
War played out for the attendees in Hall H.

00:00:51.100 --> 00:00:56.400
"There is no way in hell that we are not gonna
show you some footage."

00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:03.320
Naturally, Marvelites began speculating that
the Russos' panel could include some exclusive

00:01:03.320 --> 00:01:05.100
footage from past Marvel movies.

00:01:05.360 --> 00:01:09.619
That theory changed when the directing duo
posted another video of audio from Community,

00:01:09.619 --> 00:01:13.829
the sitcom they executive produced in the
years before they became MCU icons.

00:01:13.829 --> 00:01:16.240
"Donde, está, la biblioteca.

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:19.240
Me llamo T-Bone, la araña discoteca."

00:01:19.450 --> 00:01:23.680
Fans' minds began racing a mile a minute,
then went into overdrive with the Russo Brothers'

00:01:23.690 --> 00:01:28.729
third and most recent SDCC tease: a video
containing audio from Arrested Development,

00:01:28.729 --> 00:01:31.710
yet another television series the two worked
on pre-Marvel.

00:01:31.710 --> 00:01:34.960
In the video, Jeffrey Tambor's character delivers
his iconic mini-monologue:

00:01:35.420 --> 00:01:37.819
"How much clearer can I say?

00:01:37.820 --> 00:01:41.580
There's always money in the banana stand!”

00:01:42.120 --> 00:01:45.960
Some fans are of the opinion that the Russos
might confirm that a Community film is in

00:01:45.960 --> 00:01:49.759
the works, while others believe that they'll
announce season 6 of Arrested Development.

00:01:49.759 --> 00:01:53.470
Still, others believe that they'll offer an
update on the Arrested Development movie that's

00:01:53.470 --> 00:01:55.500
been coming together since 2009.

00:01:55.920 --> 00:01:59.899
One fan pointed out that the Russos definitely
have the money to fund a Community movie,

00:01:59.900 --> 00:02:01.640
an Arrested Development film, or both.

00:02:01.909 --> 00:02:05.880
They might even be using their earnings from
Avengers: Endgame, which has grossed over

00:02:05.880 --> 00:02:10.260
$2.78 billion worldwide as of July 16, to
revisit their old works.

00:02:10.750 --> 00:02:14.900
Any way you toss it, fans are flipping over
the Russo Brothers' pre-San Diego Comic-Con

00:02:14.900 --> 00:02:15.400
teases.

00:02:15.400 --> 00:02:18.820
But there truly is no telling exactly what
they have planned for their convention panel.

00:02:19.320 --> 00:02:24.020
All we know is that Collider's editor-in-chief
Steve Weintraub is moderating the presentation,

00:02:24.030 --> 00:02:28.410
which is officially billed as being a reflection
of the Russos' time filming Avengers: Endgame

00:02:28.410 --> 00:02:31.950
and a look into how they will transition into
"life beyond Marvel" with their production

00:02:31.950 --> 00:02:33.180
company AGBO.

00:02:33.560 --> 00:02:38.680
There's a chance that AGBO could be the studio
behind a Community movie or an Arrested Development

00:02:38.680 --> 00:02:43.360
film, and that when the panel discussion shifts
to AGBO, the Russos will unveil one or both

00:02:43.360 --> 00:02:44.360
of those projects.

00:02:44.360 --> 00:02:48.640
What likely won't be featured during "A Conversation
with the Russo Brothers" is any talk of Marvel's

00:02:48.640 --> 00:02:53.240
Phase 4 plans, since that will presumably
be reserved for Marvel Studios' Hall H panel

00:02:53.240 --> 00:02:57.000
on Saturday, July 20 at 5:15 PM PST.

00:02:57.120 --> 00:03:01.840
The notoriously secretive studio hasn't confirmed
anything about its film schedule past Spider-Man:

00:03:01.840 --> 00:03:05.820
Far From Home, the Phase 3-ender that swung
into theaters at the start of July.

00:03:05.980 --> 00:03:10.320
A handful of movies notably The Eternals and
the Black Widow solo film have already begun

00:03:10.320 --> 00:03:11.080
taking shape.

00:03:11.320 --> 00:03:14.360
But Marvel is essentially pretending that
they don't exist for the time being.

00:03:14.660 --> 00:03:18.880
Whatever happens at the Russos' personal panel,
it probably won't be MCU-related.

